.TH scrawny 1  "scrawny 0.1.0" 
.SH NAME
scrawny \- Detect and explain review\-hostile changes.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBscrawny\fR [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-path\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Detect and explain review\-hostile changes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR [default: text]
Output format: text, json, jsonl
.TP
\fB\-\-path\fR \fI<PATH>\fR [default: .]
Repository path to analyse
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
scrawny\-analyse(1)
Analyse current changes (default when no subcommand is given)
.TP
scrawny\-explain(1)
Explain why a change is considered review\-hostile, with evidence
.TP
scrawny\-suggest(1)
Generate a decomposition proposal (ranked clusters, no mutation)
.TP
scrawny\-split(1)
Construct and validate a real series of commits from the detected clusters, entirely inside a disposable temporary worktree. Never touches the current branch or checkout; nothing is merged, reset, or pushed. `\-\-apply`\-style automation onto the real branch is deliberately not implemented (Phase V territory)
.TP
scrawny\-check(1)
CI\-compatible pass/fail check against policy thresholds
.TP
scrawny\-diff(1)
Analyse a supplied diff instead of the working repository
.TP
scrawny\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH VERSION
v0.1.0
